Oh, I was referring to Channels.csv only. That's the only file RepeaterBook exports. Until recently it didn't include the APRS, latitude, longitude columns in the Channels.csv file he exported. Even though the Channels.csv file his website produced was missing the last three columns, the exported file imported into the CPS just fine, which is why I'm speculating that the addition of the Use Location column at the end of the column list won't cause any issues.<br><br>I do think it will require me to go through and check the "use location" box though for each channel in that imported Channels.csv file that included position information. That's the part I plan on testing. I'm also considering reaching back out to the Repeater Book developer to see if he can include the new "use location" column in the Channels.csv export and have the value be set to yes if the export is including position information for that particular channel, although I'm a bit hesitant to ask him for additional programming after he <em class="text-italics">just</em> added the location APRS and location columns in the Channels.csv export file.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3765">KB0PCH</a> — Wed Aug 14, 2024 2:36 pm</p><hr />
