<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I contacted the admin at RepeaterBook and sent my current code plug indicating the differences (APRS, Lat/Long and another field) and he seemed interested in helping change their format. We'll see what happens; the Lat/Long are in the GPX export so I took the time to grab the coordinates and put them in my file.</div></blockquote>Quick follow-up: The gentleman who runs RepeaterBook did add the APRS, LAT, and LOG columns to the OpenGD77 export on his site a couple of days ago. They have the position of a lot of the repeaters in the database, it will be nice to have that information in the export!</div></blockquote>I've made an update to the CPS Export/Import functionality, so that the "Use Location" check-box is now exported and imported<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/Experimental/OpenGD77CPSInstaller_R2024.08.13.01.exe" class="postlink">downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/Experimental/Op ... .13.01.exe</a><br><br>Previously the Use Location was not exported and the import function guessed whether Use Location should be used, based on whether the Lat/Long appeared to be valid.<br><br>However, I think it's better now that the "Use Location" column is being both exported and imported<br><br>I'm not sure how this affects the Repeater Book data, but ultimately its for individual operators to decided whether they want the Lat/Long for a repeater to be used or not, hence they can set that column in the spreadsheet accordingly<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Aug 13, 2024 9:31 am</p><hr />
